{"id": "goal-checklist-completes", "why": "#318: a standing goal must produce a checklist and be able to finish it. The regression was a goal born done, or one that could never be closed.", "args": ["--goal", "add a health endpoint and a test for it"], "prompt": "get the objective done", "script": [{"tool": "todo_write", "arguments": {"todos": [{"content": "add the health endpoint", "status": "in_progress"}, {"content": "add a test for it", "status": "pending"}]}}, {"tool": "todo_write", "arguments": {"todos": [{"content": "add the health endpoint", "status": "completed"}, {"content": "add a test for it", "status": "completed"}]}}, {"text": "the endpoint and its test are in"}], "assert": [{"events_at_least": {"match": {"type": "tool_call", "name": "todo_write"}, "count": 2}}, {"request_contains": {"index": -1, "text": "add the health endpoint"}}, {"request_contains": {"index": -1, "text": "completed"}}, {"final_text_contains": "the endpoint and its test are in"}]}
{"id": "standing-goal-restated", "why": "#318: --goal is a standing objective, so it has to reach the model on every call, not only the first.", "args": ["--goal", "keep the build green"], "prompt": "what should I do next", "script": [{"text": "checking"}, {"text": "still checking"}], "assert": [{"request_contains": {"index": 0, "text": "keep the build green"}}, {"request_contains": {"index": -1, "text": "keep the build green"}}]}
{"id": "todo-empty-write-noop", "why": "6300514: a todo_write with no usable items must leave the list untouched. It used to wipe the checklist, and an empty list read as completion.", "args": [], "prompt": "plan two steps, then send an empty checklist", "script": [{"tool": "todo_write", "arguments": {"todos": [{"content": "survey the call sites", "status": "pending"}, {"content": "land the fix", "status": "pending"}]}}, {"tool": "todo_write", "arguments": {"todos": []}}, {"tool": "todo_read", "arguments": {}}, {"text": "the plan is unchanged"}], "assert": [{"events_at_least": {"match": {"type": "tool_call", "name": "todo_read"}, "count": 1}}, {"request_contains": {"index": -1, "text": "survey the call sites"}}, {"request_contains": {"index": -1, "text": "land the fix"}}]}
{"id": "todo-preserves-completed", "why": "2896b32: a replace that omits an already-completed item must keep it. Omitting finished work used to delete it, erasing the record of what was done.", "args": [], "prompt": "finish one step then replace the list without it", "script": [{"tool": "todo_write", "arguments": {"todos": [{"content": "migrate the schema", "status": "completed"}, {"content": "backfill the rows", "status": "pending"}]}}, {"tool": "todo_write", "arguments": {"todos": [{"content": "backfill the rows", "status": "in_progress"}]}}, {"tool": "todo_read", "arguments": {}}, {"text": "still on the backfill"}], "assert": [{"request_contains": {"index": -1, "text": "migrate the schema"}}, {"request_contains": {"index": -1, "text": "backfill the rows"}}]}
{"id": "compaction-keeps-completed", "why": "#318: compaction mid-run must not lose the goal or the items already completed under it. The summary used to drop them and the run restarted work it had finished.", "args": ["--goal", "ship the migration"], "prompt": "start the work", "controls_after_turn": [{"type": "compact"}], "second_prompt": "keep going", "script": [{"tool": "todo_write", "arguments": {"todos": [{"content": "write the migration", "status": "completed"}, {"content": "run it against staging", "status": "pending"}]}}, {"text": "migration written"}, {"text": "summary of the session so far: the migration is written"}, {"text": "running it against staging now"}], "assert": [{"event": {"type": "compact", "ok": true}}, {"request_contains": {"index": -1, "text": "write the migration"}}, {"request_contains": {"index": -1, "text": "ship the migration"}}]}
{"id": "tool-budget-stops-the-run", "why": "A run that will not stop is worse than one that stops early. --max-tool-calls has to be enforced against the root agent, not just advertised.", "args": ["--max-tool-calls", "2"], "prompt": "keep calling the todo tool", "script": [{"tool": "todo_read", "arguments": {}}, {"tool": "todo_read", "arguments": {}}, {"tool": "todo_read", "arguments": {}}, {"tool": "todo_read", "arguments": {}}, {"text": "stopping"}], "assert": [{"events_at_most": {"match": {"type": "tool_call_started"}, "count": 2}}]}
